  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "57db63be-f094-418a-ad72-8c63b54fa3f5",
      "name": "Template Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -480,
        464
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 700,
        "height": 1056,
        "content": "## 📧 Route Support Emails to WhatsApp Based on Urgency\n\n## Who's it for\nSmall businesses whose support inbox gets a mix of urgent issues, routine questions, and newsletters/spam, and who want urgent stuff surfaced immediately instead of sitting in an inbox until someone happens to check it.\n\n## How it works\nEvery new email is classified by AI into urgent, routine, or spam. Urgent emails trigger an immediate WhatsApp alert to the owner and get logged. Routine emails are logged but held back, not sent one by one. Spam and newsletters are logged and otherwise ignored. Once a day, a separate scheduled run collects every routine email that hasn't been included in a digest yet, and sends one combined WhatsApp summary instead of a flood of individual notifications.\n\n## How to set up\n1. Connect your Gmail credentials to the trigger.\n2. Connect your Groq or Gemini API credentials to the Chat Model node.\n3. Connect your Supabase credentials and create the table described in the sticky note near the Log Email node.\n4. Connect your WhatsApp Business Cloud credentials to both send nodes.\n5. Open both Set Configuration nodes (one per trigger) and fill in your WhatsApp phone number ID, owner's WhatsApp number, and Supabase table name.\n6. Set your preferred digest time in the Schedule Trigger.\n7. Activate the workflow.\n\n## Requirements\n- Gmail account\n- Groq or Gemini API key\n- Supabase project\n- WhatsApp Business Cloud API access\n\n## How to customize\nEdit the classification prompt to change what counts as urgent for your business. Adjust the digest's run time, or add a second daily digest run if once a day isn't often enough."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "eb7d1e85-8465-416c-96c2-0cb9be36cda5",
